<concept_spec>

concept ProjectApplication

purpose
  manage learner applications to projects with approval workflow

state
  a set of ProjectApplications with
    a projectId String
    an applicantName String
    an applicantEmail String
    an optional applicantImage String
    a linkedinUrl String
    a message String
    an optional videoUrl String
    a status String
    an appliedAt Date
    an optional reviewedAt Date
    an optional reviewedBy String
    a createdAt Date
    an updatedAt Date

actions
  apply(projectId: String, applicantName: String, applicantEmail: String, linkedinUrl: String, message: String, applicantImage: String?, videoUrl: String?) -> ProjectApplication | {error}
    - create new project application
    - validate required fields
    - check if project exists
    - check if user has already applied (one application per user per project)
    - set status to "pending"
    - return application with generated id and timestamps

  approve(id: String, reviewedBy: String) -> ProjectApplication | {error}
    - approve pending application
    - requires expert, educator, manager, or platform_admin role
    - set status to "approved"
    - set reviewedAt to current timestamp
    - set reviewedBy to reviewer email
    - return updated application

  reject(id: String, reviewedBy: String) -> ProjectApplication | {error}
    - reject pending application
    - requires expert, educator, manager, or platform_admin role
    - set status to "rejected"
    - set reviewedAt to current timestamp
    - set reviewedBy to reviewer email
    - return updated application

  withdraw(id: String, applicantEmail: String) -> ProjectApplication | {error}
    - withdraw own application
    - only applicant can withdraw
    - delete application record
    - return success status

queries
  _getById(id: String) -> [ProjectApplication]
    - return application by identifier

  _getByProject(projectId: String) -> [ProjectApplication]
    - return all applications for a project

  _getByApplicant(applicantEmail: String) -> [ProjectApplication]
    - return all applications from a specific applicant

  _getByStatus(status: String) -> [ProjectApplication]
    - return applications with specified status (pending/approved/rejected)

  _getPendingApplications() -> [ProjectApplication]
    - return all pending applications requiring review

  _getApprovedApplications() -> [ProjectApplication]
    - return all approved applications

  _getAppliedProjects(applicantEmail: String) -> [{projectId: String, status: String}]
    - return map of projectId to application status for a learner
    - used to display applied/approved/rejected badges in UI

  _checkExistingApplication(projectId: String, applicantEmail: String) -> [ProjectApplication]
    - check if user has already applied to a project

operational principle
  Learners apply to projects and applications must be approved by experts, educators, managers, or admins. After apply(project: "p1", email: "user@example.com", ...), the status is "pending". After approve(application: "a1", reviewer: "expert@example.com"), then _getAppliedProjects(email: "user@example.com") shows "p1" with status "approved". Applications enforce unique constraint (projectId, applicantEmail).

</concept_spec>
